## 💡 Task 4 — Business Insights

### 🔥 Insight 1 — Tables Are a Profit Black Hole
Tables generate **$207K in revenue** yet lose **$17,725**.
With an average discount of **26.1%** — the highest in the catalog — every Tables order is statistically unprofitable.

### ⚠️ Insight 2 — Discounts Are Hurting, Not Helping
Aggressive discounting is being used as a volume driver but is destroying margins.
Orders above 50% discount lose **$76.5K cumulatively**. The strategy is backfiring.

### 📍 Insight 3 — Central Region Is the Weak Link
Central earns only **$39.6K profit on $500K sales** — a 7.9% margin, barely half that of the West (14.9%).
Over-reliance on discounted Furniture is likely the root cause.

### 🏆 Insight 4 — Copiers & Technology Are the Stars
Copiers deliver a **37.2% margin** — the best in the business.
Technology earns **$145K profit on $836K sales**. Expanding this category is the fastest margin recovery path.

### 🗺️ Insight 5 — Texas & Ohio Drag National Numbers
These two states alone lose **$42,710 per year**. No regional pricing strategy appears to be active.

### 📦 Insight 6 — Furniture Is Near-Breakeven at Scale
With **$741K in revenue** and only **$18,422 in profit**, Furniture consumes operational resources (warehouse, logistics, support) while returning almost nothing financially.

